 devastating we worked so  hard and  kept going with the chemo to get to that  point  only for covid to hit and then it all  changed and  the up got cancelled obviously your  operation is your best  your best chance you've got when you  live in the cancer adrian's cancer is  now  terminal another indirect consequence of  the pandemic  what we are starting to discover in  streets and neighborhoods and households  around the country  is that the nature of normal death is  changing in the face of this pandemic so  deaths that aren't directly or  indirectly caused by covert 19  are still happening differently and  that's something that no single chart  can show you  as britain steals itself for a second  surge of the virus  it is yet another reminder that we're  only beginning to understand the  consequences of this disease  for our lives and our deaths  ed conway sky news
 

